ions","group":"Dark Side Traditions","era":"Imperial era (19 BBY–4 ABY)","description":"Dark side agents of the Empire, trained by Vader to hunt post-Order 66 Jedi survivors.","draws_from":""},{"name":"Prophets of the Dark Side","section":"Force Traditions","group":"Dark Side Traditions","era":"Imperial era (19 BBY–4 ABY)","description":"Fanatical dark side seers serving Palpatine as interpreters of Sith prophecy.","draws_from":""},{"name":"Dark Jedi","section":"Force Traditions","group":"Dark Side Traditions","era":"Multiple eras","description":"Fallen Jedi who embraced the dark side independently, outside formal Sith lineage.","draws_from":""},{"name":"Disciples of Ragnos","section":"Force Traditions","group":"Dark Side Traditions","era":"New Republic / NJO (4 ABY+)","description":"A cult dedicated to resurrecting Sith Lord Marka Ragnos by siphoning Force nexus energy.","draws_from":""},{"name":"Mecrosa Order","section":"Force Traditions","group":"Dark Side Traditions","era":"Old Republic (5000–1000 BBY)","description":"Dark side assassins embedded within Tapani nobility, blending poison craft with Force.","draws_from":"The noble houses of the Tapani sector."},{"name":"Galactic Republic","section":"Governments, Militaries and Powers","group":"Governments and States","era":"c. 25,053 BBY–19 BBY","description":"The democratic union of member worlds ruled from Coruscant by the Senate and the Supreme Chancellor, and defended for most of its history by the Jedi.","draws_from":""},{"name":"Confederacy of Independent Systems","section":"Governments, Militaries and Powers","group":"Governments and States","era":"24–19 BBY","description":"The Separatists: systems and corporations that seceded from the Republic under Count Dooku and fought the Clone Wars.","draws_from":""},{"name":"Galactic Empire","section":"Governments, Militaries and Powers","group":"Governments and States","era":"19 BBY–4 ABY; fragmented until 11 ABY","description":"Palpatine's New Order, which replaced